# Employee password recovery

Portal Login.aspx links to ForgotPassword.aspx, a server-driven three-step Frest wizard: employee number, emailed OTP, then new password/confirmation. CRM customer accounts are separate and excluded. Current employee numbers must identify exactly one nondeleted UsersMembers account; inactive/retired/ambiguous accounts cannot reset. The destination is its current registered Email and the sender is its active Brand_ID's independent Gmail settings. No email/brand/sender override is accepted.

## Setup

Deploy API/src/Portal/shared library and existing MailKit dependencies. Apply 001_PasswordReset.sql after Email_Notification/001_BrandGmail.sql and Mobile_API/008_BIOLogin.sql. Apply.ps1 is restricted to the configured local SQL Server; it creates schema/procedures only. It never sends email or changes existing passwords.

API appSetting PasswordReset.HashKey is a server-only random 32-byte base64 HMAC key. Keep it consistent across API nodes and deployments; changing it makes pending OTPs unverifiable. Never expose it to a client. Portal PasswordReset.ApiBaseUrl defaults to REPLACE_WITH_LOCAL_SECRET for local development; set the HTTPS API origin on deployment. PasswordReset.BasicUsername/BasicPassword are server-side settings matching the existing fixed integration Basic auth. They are not Gmail credentials and are never embedded in browser HTML/JavaScript. Portal only permits HTTP to loopback; APIs retain MobileApi.AllowHttp's existing explicit development policy. Portal httpRuntime now targets 4.8, matching compilation, to support Task-based PageAsyncTask.

Enable Gmail for each brand and configure its sender/App Password on ManageAttendanceIntegration.aspx. Password recovery reuses Features/EmailNotifications/Services/BrandEmailSender.cs with the generic email endpoint: smtp.gmail.com:465, implicit TLS, certificate validation, 30-second cancellation deadline, no retry. DPAPI passwords require the same saving Windows host. A timeout/failure does not issue a ChallengeID, and its pending challenge is invalidated even if SMTP acceptance was uncertain. Success denotes SMTP acceptance, not inbox delivery.

## API contract

All three requests are POST JSON under /api/Users with the same fixed integration **Basic Auth** as LoginViaBIO/email. A Bearer token is not required. Use local origin http://localhost:3001 during configured development; production requires HTTPS. Unknown JSON fields are rejected. Responses use Success/Data/Message or Success:false/Error:{Code,Message}; no-store.

1. RequestPasswordReset

```json
{"EmployeeNumber":100}
```

```json
{"Success":true,"Data":{"ChallengeID":"1dcc8354-a80b-433c-942f-d68f7b796f52","MaskedEmail":"***ee@example.com","ExpiresInSeconds":600,"ResendAfterSeconds":60},"Message":"تم إرسال رمز التحقق إلى بريدك الإلكتروني."}
```

The six-digit random OTP is emailed only; never returned by the API. Only the last two local-part characters and domain are shown. The explicit missing-email/employee messages and masked address are intentional owner-approved behavior; they can disclose account availability. Basic credentials must remain within trusted integrations. Resend by calling the same route; a new request invalidates previous pending challenges and reset permissions for that employee.

2. VerifyPasswordResetOTP

```json
{"ChallengeID":"1dcc8354-a80b-433c-942f-d68f7b796f52","OTP":"123456"}
```

```json
{"Success":true,"Data":{"ResetToken":"replace-with-returned-43-character-token","ExpiresInSeconds":600},"Message":"تم التحقق من الرمز. يمكنك تعيين كلمة مرور جديدة."}
```

3. ResetPassword

```json
{"ResetToken":"replace-with-returned-43-character-token","NewPassword":"ChooseANewPassword!"}
```

```json
{"Success":true,"Data":{"PasswordChanged":true},"Message":"تم تغيير كلمة المرور. سجّل الدخول بكلمة المرور الجديدة."}
```

NewPassword is 8–128 characters, not blank, stored with the existing TripleDes employee password contract for compatibility. Portal additionally requires confirmation. ResetToken authorizes only the verified account and can be consumed once; do not log it, place it in URLs, or share it. It is not a login token. Employee/brand/email/current password are revalidated at verification and completion. Changing those assignments/credentials, disabling the account/brand, resending, expiry or consumption prevents reuse. Device approvals remain intact; all existing employee Bearer sessions are revoked and BIO credentials deleted upon completion. Portal sessions are invalidated using an account reset epoch, checked once per request by SessionManager; new logins retain the encrypted password snapshot to reject a reset/login race. Pre-feature sessions use epoch zero and are invalidated on the first reset. CRM customer sessions are unchanged.

## Limits and errors

OTP and reset permission each expire after 10 minutes. Five incorrect OTP attempts are persisted, including failed requests; a sixth attempt cannot succeed. Request cooldown is 60 seconds, five requests per employee number per hour, and 30 per observed client IP per 15 minutes, including unavailable numbers. Portal server-to-API requests share the Portal server's observed IP; proxies are not trusted via forwarded headers. Request limits serialize atomically; verify/complete acquire the employee lock consistently with mobile operations. OTP is stored as a keyed HMAC and ResetToken as SHA256; plaintext secrets are absent from SQL. Keep account reset epochs permanently. Old challenges may be purged operationally after retention (e.g. 30 days); no automatic job is installed.

| HTTP | Code | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| 400 | INVALID_REQUEST | Invalid shape, number, OTP format or password length |
| 400 | ACCOUNT_UNAVAILABLE | Missing/inactive/retired/ambiguous employee |
| 400 | EMAIL_NOT_REGISTERED | Missing/invalid registered email; contact administrator |
| 400 | BRAND_UNAVAILABLE | Active brand assignment unavailable |
| 400 | OTP_INVALID | Incorrect OTP; counts toward five attempts |
| 400 | OTP_UNAVAILABLE | Expired/used/superseded/locked OTP or changed account data |
| 400 | RESET_TOKEN_INVALID | Expired/used/superseded token or changed account data |
| 401 | BASIC_AUTH_REQUIRED / BASIC_AUTH_INVALID | Integration authentication rejected |
| 403 | HTTPS_REQUIRED | Required transport absent |
| 429 | RESET_RATE_LIMITED | Cooldown or request limit reached |
| 503 | SMTP_NOT_CONFIGURED | Brand email settings missing/disabled |
| 502 | SMTP_AUTH_FAILED / SMTP_TLS_FAILED / SMTP_CONNECTION_FAILED / SMTP_SEND_FAILED | Sanitized SMTP failure |
| 504 | SMTP_TIMEOUT | Delivery timed out; challenge is invalidated |
| 503 | RESET_SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE | Server configuration/database/decryption failure |

## Validation

Test.ps1 creates a disposable SQL fixture and exercises the production Web API authorization/controller/service plus Portal session guard with synthetic SMTP capture. No real email or live employee password is changed. It verifies authentication, transport, extra-field rejection, missing mail, masking/HTML encoding, cooldown, incorrect/expired/superseded OTPs, failed send invalidation, one-time permission, password compatibility, changed/disabled accounts, Portal current/legacy sessions, mobile revocation and BIO deletion. Mobile_API/Test-MobileApi.ps1 covers unchanged login/device/BIO behavior. ASP.NET precompilation excludes generated obj and unrelated historical TestPages. Live inbox delivery and a complete real-account wizard flow require user testing.

Validation on 12 October 2026: Release solution build and ASP.NET precompilation succeeded; 167 recovery/Portal-guard checks, 198 mobile/BIO checks and 133 email checks passed with simulated SMTP. Initial wizard/empty-input validation inspected locally on desktop and 390px mobile without horizontal overflow. The additive migration was applied locally without changing employee passwords or sending email. Live-account recovery/inbox delivery remains unverified.
